The Arithmetic Logic Unit was successfully designed and simulated using Verilog HDL. All arithmetic and logical operations produced the expected outputs during simulation. The waveform analysis confirmed the proper functioning of the ALU for every select input condition.

This project provided practical understanding of Verilog programming, combinational circuit design, testbench creation, and digital circuit simulation. It also helped in understanding the internal working of processors and digital systems.

Overall, the simulation was completed successfully, and the project achieved all intended objectives.
